---
// website/src/pages/index.astro — the site's front page (website plan, Task W1.4; redesign
// parts P1, P5 and P8; the owner's approved board `website/design-ref/HomeV3.dc.html`,
// 2026-10-20, which supersedes the draft "Home, draft 2 (slider)", 2026-10-19).
//
// **The page is five blocks, and the board says which five**: the hero — the title, the prompt
// line and the one-line promise, with the call to action the site has always had — then the
// slider whose three tabs are how it is to use, why it is worth it and what it looks like
// running, then the run's four steps as a band, then the grid of what a run leaves behind, then
// the closing call to action with the install command. The page before the board was three
// blocks: the hero, the slider and the button. The board splits the run out of the slider's
// first panel into a band of its own and gives the page a grid of what a run leaves behind, so
// this file renders `Hero`, `HomeSlider`, `HomeRunBand`, `HomeWhatYouGet` and `HomeInstall`.
//
// **What left the page, and where it went.** The chat's illustration is the slider's first
// panel — the three steps a reader takes, each with a line of the README under it — so
// `AgentChat.astro` is gone rather than hidden: a component no page renders is a component
// whose build-time guards no longer run. The four-step flow left the site with the owner's
// ruling of 2026-10-20, which retires `ArchitectureDiagram.astro`: the run is
// `/how-it-works/`'s own drawing, and the band above the grid is the homepage's summary of it —
// four names and four lines, not the picture, which `website/test/home.mjs` refuses here on
// purpose. The benefits are still `Benefits.astro`, rendered by the slider's second panel; and
// the two install cards are the button above the one command most readers run, with every path
// still laid out on `/getting-started/`.
//
// Every block reads what it renders through the content pipeline (W1.3) and holds it to the
// repository; this page holds no fact of its own.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro'
import HomeSlider from '../components/HomeSlider.astro'
import HomeRunBand from '../components/HomeRunBand.astro'
import HomeWhatYouGet from '../components/HomeWhatYouGet.astro'
import HomeInstall from '../components/HomeInstall.astro'
---

<Base title="Fugaro">
  {/* Five top-level blocks, each carrying its own gutter and its own room below: `main:has(>
      .hero)` drops `main`'s padding on this page, so no block adds a top padding on top of the
      block above's bottom one, and the gap between two of them is one padding rather than two
      (`website/test/base-styles.mjs`'s `homeRhythmFailures` reads the five at 1280, 768 and
      375 px). */}
  <Hero />
  <HomeSlider />
  <HomeRunBand />
  <HomeWhatYouGet />
  <HomeInstall />
</Base>
